+---
+id: task-002-fix-coupon-base-coupon-expiry-day-and-report-shipping-vat-question
+type: task
+title: "Fix coupon base, coupon expiry day and report shipping VAT question"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Fix coupon base, coupon expiry day and report shipping VAT question
+
+Three reports from customers and finance, checked against the rules in `README.md`.
+
+## 1. Coupon applied to the gross amount, not after volume discounts (finance)
+
+- Twelve notebooks at €5.00 with a 10% coupon come to €48.00 of goods; expected €48.60.
+- Rule: "a coupon ... applies to the order's subtotal after volume discounts" (Discounts).
+- Cause: `priceOrder` in `src/pricing.ts` computes the coupon from `grossTotal`, before the volume
+  discount. The 10% coupon takes €6.00 (of €60.00) instead of €5.40 (of €54.00).
+- Acceptance: the coupon's base is the subtotal after volume discounts, for both percentage and fixed
+  coupons. The example above gives goods of €48.60. A fixed coupon still never takes off more than that
+  subtotal, and the 50% cap on all discounts still holds.
+
+## 2. Coupon refused on its last day (customer, Luca)
+
+- AUTUMN is valid until 30 November; an order placed on 30 November is refused as expired.
+- Rule: "A coupon is valid from its first day to its last day, both included" (Discounts); "Periods
+  given as 'from … to …' include both days" (Money and dates).
+- Cause: `Coupons.redeemable` in `src/coupons.ts` tests `date >= validUntil` for expiry, which excludes
+  the last day.
+- Acceptance: an order on `validUntil` uses the coupon; an order the day after is refused as expired.
+
+## 3. VAT on shipping (customer, Anna) — not changed, needs a decision
+
+- Anna's receipt shows €1.08 VAT on €4.90 of shipping. She asks that delivery carry no VAT.
+- The README states the rule: "Shipping is subject to VAT at the standard rate (22%), shown on its own
+  line of the receipt" (VAT). The code, `shippingVat` in `src/tax.ts`, implements that rule, so the
+  receipt is correct under the documented rules.
+- The README says "When the code and this list disagree, this list is right", and a change of VAT
+  treatment is a business rule, not a code defect. This task does not change it. The rule needs a
+  decision by the business owner before the README and the code can change.
+
+## Traceability
+
+- Requirements: the Discounts and Money and dates rules in `README.md`; the VAT rule on shipping is
+  quoted above and left as it is.
+- Tests to cover items 1 and 2 are added under `test/`.
